    "field": "Global energy budgets",
    "problem": "Climate models exhibit persistent biases in tropical precipitation, which are hypothesized to result from an inaccurate representation of the hemispheric energy balance and the resulting cross-equatorial energy transport.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method to construct new estimates of the hemispheric energy balance by assembling observational data on radiative fluxes and ocean heat content and reviewing climate model simulations to investigate resulting tropical precipitation biases.",
    "task": "The task is to present new estimates of the Earth\u2019s hemispheric energy and water balances using observational data and to review climate model simulations to investigate the role of these hemispheric asymmetries in causing biases in tropical precipitation.",
